# What must NEVER reach the image.
#
# `COPY . .` copies the build context, and the context is the working tree — .gitignore
# has no say in it. Without this file the deployed image carried .env (every production
# secret in plaintext), key.md, the Firebase service-account key under _excluded/, the
# development SQLite database and seven full git worktrees: 1.01 GB of context, ~900 MB
# of it dead weight, and every credential readable by anyone who can pull the image or
# open a console on the machine.
#
# Secrets reach the container through `fly secrets set` (see DEPLOY_CHECKLIST.md), never
# through a file in the repository.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
key.md
*.pem
*.key
*firebase*adminsdk*.json
_excluded/

# Local databases and developer state
db.sqlite3
*.sqlite3
.git/
.gitignore
.claude/
.cursor/
.vscode/
.agent/
.agents/
.venv/
venv/
.DS_Store

# Build and test artifacts. staticfiles/ is REGENERATED by collectstatic during the
# build; copying a local one in would ship stale hashed assets.
staticfiles/
media/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.log

# Not part of the running service
tests/
scripts/
docs/
.github/
*.md
!DEPLOY_CHECKLIST.md
